From c98e4ae83bd15bd9a1e3f12dccfca55520aa4621 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lumnus <lumnus.org@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 01:34:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 33/53] B70-PLE-PRELOAD: preload the rank's INT8 PLE rows into
 the pinned NVMe row cache (B70_PLE_INT8_NVME_PRELOAD=1)

Opt-in (default 0). At init, when the rank's cache capacity >= its owned rows,
read the owned row range (one contiguous byte range of the table) into the
pinned slab with sequential O_DIRECT chunks (B70_PLE_INT8_NVME_PRELOAD_THREADS,
default 4; B70_PLE_INT8_NVME_PRELOAD_CHUNK_MIB, default 64) through page-aligned
bounces, then PleRowCache.mark_all_resident(): slot r = row r, the slots carry
a pinned epoch CLOCK never picks, the tail stays free, and lookup() skips the
ref/epoch writes. Zero NVMe reads per step afterwards; a miss, if one ever
reached install(), takes a free tail slot and never displaces a preloaded row.
Capacity < owned rows: one warning, normal cache. The boot sample rows (O_DIRECT
row reads) are compared byte for byte against the preloaded slab. One log line
per rank: rows, GiB, seconds, GB/s.
